#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# cases

#% text
# `cases(xs, p)` gives the elements of the list `xs` that match the pattern `p`.

#% text
# `cases(xs, p -> r)` gives `r` for each element matching `p`, with the pattern's names bound.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Patterns: `_` anything, `x_` named, `x_: T` of a type, `f(x_)` by head, `p when c` with a condition.

#% item
# Only the elements of `xs` are tested, not their parts.

#% item
# `select` is the counterpart with a test function.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
cases([1, a, 2.5, b, 3], _: Int)
#% output
#= [1, 3]

#% cell
cases([f(1), g(2), f(3)], f(_))
#% output
#= [f(1), f(3)]

#% cell
cases([f(1), g(2), f(3)], f(k_) -> k^2)
#% output
#= [1, 9]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A condition on the match:

#% cell
cases([3, -1, 4, -5], k_ when k < 0)
#% output
#= [-1, -5]

#% text
# Rules picked out of a list:

#% cell
cases([x -> 1, y -> 2, x -> 3], (x -> v_) -> v)
#% output
#= [1, 3]

#% text
# Pairs with a given first element:

#% cell
cases([[1, a], [2, b], [1, c]], [1, s_] -> s)
#% output
#= [a, c]

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The exponents of the powers of `x` in a sum's terms:

#% cell
cases([x^2, 3, x^5, y], x^k_ -> k)
#% output
#= [2, 5]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `count` counts the matches, `position` gives where they are:

#% cell
xs = [1, a, 2, b]
[count(xs, _: Int), position(xs, _: Int)]
#% output
#= [2, [[1], [3]]]

#% text
# `select` with a type test does the same as a typed pattern:

#% cell
select([1, a, 2, b], is_integer)
#% output
#= [1, 2]

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A rule as the pattern binds to the right: write the pattern of a rule in parentheses:

#% cell
cases([x -> 1, y -> 2], x -> v_ -> v)
#% output
#= []

#% text
# The type names `Str` and `Sym` are not accepted in a pattern here; test with `is_string` or `is_symbol` through `select` instead:

#% cell
cases(["id", 4, "name", 2.5], _: Str)
#% output
#= ["id", "name"]

#% cell
select(["id", 4, "name", 2.5], is_string)
#% output
#= ["id", "name"]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `select`, `count`, `position`, `rewrite`, `member_of`
